#FLAG long
SET UTF8
TRY abcdefghijklmnoprstuvwyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPRSTUVWYZ

# Key principle: Never mix tense flags
# In your .dic file, create separate entries:
# lya/[present tense flag][other flags]      # Present tense: produces "bagulya", "gubalya", etc.
# lya/[past tense flag][other flags]        # Near past tense: produces "baagulya", "gubalya", etc.
# This prevents "babaagulya" from being generated because tense flags will never combine on the same word.

# Lets first apply the 1st, 2nd and 3rd person prefixes both singular and plural
# Commented this out and combined them with subject markers
# PFX A Y 6
# PFX A 0 n .
# PFX A 0 o .
# PFX A 0 a .
# PFX A 0 tu .
# PFX A 0 mu .
# PFX A 0 ba .

# Reflexive verb form
PFX B Y 6
PFX B 0 nee .
PFX B 0 wee .
PFX B 0 yee .
PFX B 0 twe .
PFX B 0 mwe .
PFX B 0 bee .

# Negating the verb
PFX C Y 6 
PFX C 0 si .
PFX C 0 to .
PFX C 0 ta .
PFX C 0 tetu .
PFX C 0 temu .
PFX C 0 teba .

# Negating the reflexive verb form
PFX D Y 6
PFX D 0 see .
PFX D 0 tewee .
PFX D 0 teyee .
PFX D 0 tetwe .
PFX D 0 temwe .
PFX D 0 tebee .

# subjects markers in present and very near past tense 
PFX E Y 25
PFX E 0 n [^b]
PFX E 0 m [b]
PFX E 0 o .
PFX E l nd [l]
PFX E 0 a .
PFX E 0 tu .
PFX E 0 mu .
PFX E 0 ba .
PFX E 0 a [^aeiou]
PFX E 0 ba .
PFX E 0 gu .
PFX E 0 gi .
PFX E 0 e [^aeiou]
PFX E 0 zi .
PFX E 0 ki .
PFX E 0 bi .
PFX E 0 li .
PFX E 0 ga .
PFX E 0 ka .
PFX E 0 bu .
PFX E 0 lu .
PFX E 0 zi .
PFX E 0 ku .
PFX E 0 ga .
PFX E 0 tu .

# subject markers in near past tense
PFX G Y 19
PFX G 0 nna .
PFX G 0 wa .
PFX G 0 ya .
PFX G 0 twa .
PFX G 0 mwa .
PFX G 0 baa .
PFX G 0 gwa .
PFX G 0 gya .
PFX G 0 zaa .
PFX G 0 kyaa .
PFX G 0 byaa .
PFX G 0 lyaa .
PFX G 0 gaa .
PFX G 0 kaa .
PFX G 0 bw .
PFX G 0 lwa .
PFX G 0 kwaa .
PFX G 0 gaa .
PFX G 0 twaa .

# subject markers for the distant past tense
PFX J Y 20
PFX J 0 nn .
PFX J 0 wa .
PFX J 0 ya .
PFX J 0 twa .
PFX J 0 mwa .
PFX J 0 baa .
PFX J 0 gwa .
